                "entry_id": "86f5d943-7f9e-3417-8ba5-ae23010aba9d",
                "word": "gamedev",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "5b8c9912-e474-403e-a043-346540b52ee7",
                        "entry_id": "86f5d943-7f9e-3417-8ba5-ae23010aba9d",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "gamedevs"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c1366594-27ce-349b-a5df-975e1d5dde52",
                        "entry_id": "86f5d943-7f9e-3417-8ba5-ae23010aba9d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Game development."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "informal",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "688f275a-4b2a-4a12-8365-d9c4b68895ba",
                                "sense_id": "c1366594-27ce-349b-a5df-975e1d5dde52",
                                "text": "My first real gamedev job … we were three guys … Now I work for a big company, doing AAA titles, but I feel bitter, yes there is some excitement, but then the teams are 100-150 people, you got not one platform but 4-5 (old-gen + next-gen), and one of it launch title. It’s a hell ride. (Chaos Engine, 2006)"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "600dd49d-80a9-4295-bb48-5d043f3d8f3d",
                                "sense_id": "c1366594-27ce-349b-a5df-975e1d5dde52",
                                "text": "Assembly also hosts a gamedev competition which attracted 19 entries this year."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b934f97e-a819-469b-b299-53a32e366640",
                                "sense_id": "c1366594-27ce-349b-a5df-975e1d5dde52",
                                "text": "Real gamedev is impossible without fair amount of math. […] This book covers many gamedev algorithms and optimizations, most of which are not limited to JavaScript. […] I encourage you to join and share your gamedev assets for free—the developer community will be most grateful. […] It doesn’t make much sense to write this class step by step, since the code doesn’t really have anything to do with gamedev-specific algorithms."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7a65f38f-68b5-4515-8b65-5e920f0c946c",
                                "sense_id": "c1366594-27ce-349b-a5df-975e1d5dde52",
                                "text": "Gamedev images from Twitter"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "873985de-1316-4f39-ad80-8df368674e47",
                                "sense_id": "c1366594-27ce-349b-a5df-975e1d5dde52",
                                "text": "Kent, who started his own business called Om Games, plans to attend the Rochester Institute of Technology in New York in the fall to study game design and development with a business minor. Kent, a member of the Columbus-based Central Ohio Gamedev Group, hopes to continue the business through college but wants to focus on school."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9dfa4651-ec70-477e-85ea-9d7a9023afe1",
                                "sense_id": "c1366594-27ce-349b-a5df-975e1d5dde52",
                                "text": "Rosman has continued to run monthly meetups since 2009 and says that’s how she became known as “Melbourne’s gamedev aunty.” […] “As for what the environment is like, our gamedev is about keeping things fun and professional; never uptight.[…]”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fa10f01a-b8ce-4d05-9117-2c9202996454",
                                "sense_id": "c1366594-27ce-349b-a5df-975e1d5dde52",
                                "text": "I believe it can provide you a lot of value, so all I ask from you is a few minutes of your time, so I can share with you why it can be beneficial to you and your gamedev journey. If you haven’t read it yet, you might enjoy GAMEDEV: 10 Steps to Making Your First Game Successful."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c57f4219-e5d5-4111-bcbe-1156b2a7818d",
                                "sense_id": "c1366594-27ce-349b-a5df-975e1d5dde52",
                                "text": "The gamedev community is really a small world of really cool people."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c2192900-4137-46fd-a5fd-4273531104d0",
                                "sense_id": "c1366594-27ce-349b-a5df-975e1d5dde52",
                                "text": "Jump into hardware hacking and gamedev at the same time with a purpose-built handheld that uses MicroPython as its game development platform"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "74323f2f-fd57-33ae-aa9b-798ac53e5363",
                        "entry_id": "86f5d943-7f9e-3417-8ba5-ae23010aba9d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A game developer."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "informal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "32edc4f0-0357-4a76-b9da-d345c24b8402",
                                "sense_id": "74323f2f-fd57-33ae-aa9b-798ac53e5363",
                                "text": "Gamedevs share code, war stories, screenshots, videos, and links to their games, and the conversation regarding tools, languages, and algorithms is very active."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ca553f51-0c38-4b13-9a11-9914c1913625",
                                "sense_id": "74323f2f-fd57-33ae-aa9b-798ac53e5363",
                                "text": "Come and be inspired by your peers’ game audio journeys both present and future, join the conversation, network with other gamedevs and party by the seaside. […] Descriptor: A tour of the most common pitfalls unprepared gamedevs encounter on dialogue projects for videogames."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b3cac8b9-c660-4243-a9ef-117f11db9950",
                                "sense_id": "74323f2f-fd57-33ae-aa9b-798ac53e5363",
                                "text": "Dreams’ creative range is astonishing, and it’s possible to make any style of game in minutes, whether it’s a marble run, a city sim, or a rhythm-action minigame within another game. Ettouney hopes this may encourage jaded gamedevs to experiment more: […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
